The UR-OS simulator is a Java-based application designed to include all the main active components of a computer system in order to replicate the behavior of an operating system and its interaction with hardware elements such as the processor, memory, and file system. This modular simulator allows users to select and combine different algorithms for each function. This deliverable extends the free memory management function of the simulator -- previously limited to First Fit -- with two new hole-selection strategies for contiguous allocation: \textbf{Best Fit}, which assigns the smallest free hole that is large enough for the request, and \textbf{Worst Fit}, which assigns the largest free hole. Both strategies were integrated into the operating system configuration, validated inside the full simulation, and compared against First Fit on controlled fragmentation scenarios, with every allocation independently verified by a manual, step-by-step trace of the free-hole list.
\end{minipage}

