\subsection{Summary}

Best Fit meets the expected behavior. In Scenario A it is the only strategy that satisfies all five requests, because it serves the 90-byte request from the 100-byte hole and leaves the 400-byte hole intact for the later large requests. The cost of the policy is also visible: that same decision leaves a 10-byte fragment at $[490, 500)$ that is practically unusable, which is the typical ``splinter'' effect of Best Fit.

