\subsection{Summary}

Worst Fit meets the expected behavior: it always cuts from the largest hole. In Scenario B this is exactly what makes it the only strategy that satisfies all three requests: after serving 150 bytes from the 400-byte hole, a 250-byte hole remains, which later fits the 250-byte request exactly. In Scenario A, however, the same policy destroys the 400-byte hole with the very first (small) request, and when the 180-byte request arrives there are 240 free bytes but no single hole larger than 100 bytes.

